 "_doc": "Per plug-in choices the generator can't make from the source alone. wide: members the fast variant keeps in double, with every statement that touches them, because a long sum in single precision drifts from upstream. phase: wide members that only grow by a step and wrap to zero, which the fast variant keeps in Q4.60 fixed point, so adding the step costs no double arithmetic. fast: false runs upstream's arithmetic in the fast slot too, for a plug-in whose single-precision loop measured outside the bar (fast_error: its worst case, in int16 steps). skip: why a plug-in isn't carried at all.",
